id: pm-suhxny
title: "The public-surface gate enumerates its own hand-written entrypoint list, so two published code exports ship ungoverned and ./cli publishes 86 internal functions as typed API"
description: "scripts/sdk-surface-snapshot.mjs iterates a frozen ENTRYPOINT_CLASSIFICATIONS map of ten keys and looks each one up in package.json exports. It never iterates the export map, so coverage is proven in one direction only: every classified entrypoint must exist in the package, and no package entrypoint must be classified."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[5]: "area:release","area:sdk",gate-denominator,governance,surface
created_at: "2026-08-16T10:05:42.492Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-16T10:51:44.247Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-16T10:51:43.567Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-16T10:51:43.567Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
acceptance_criteria: "The surface generator derives its denominator from package.json exports and refuses to build while any export declaring a types path is unclassified; A negative control proves the refusal fires when a new code export is added and passes once it is classified; Every published code export appears in sdk/public-surface.json, with alias entries recording their target instead of duplicating symbols; The ./cli entrypoint's exported symbols are recorded so a change to what it exposes is a classified surface change; The disposition of publishing _testOnly through ./cli is recorded rather than implicitly blessed"
parent: pm-usfg
risk: high
confidence: high
resolution: "Replaced the hand-written entrypoint enumeration with an export-map-derived denominator, added alias target verification, and brought both previously ungoverned code exports under the surface contract."
expected_result: Every entry in the published package export map is governed by the public-surface compatibility gate.
actual_result: "Ten of twelve code exports are governed. The root export and ./cli are invisible to the gate, and ./cli ships 86 internal functions with type declarations."
