  pm-te6elw,discovered_from,"2026-08-16T10:40:22.805Z","harness:claude-code","cli:update:dep",detected
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-16T10:51:42.915Z","harness:claude-code","Evidence. Measurement: package.json declares 12 code exports (entries with a types path); sdk/public-surface.json governed 10. Ungoverned: the root '.' and './cli'. dist/cli/main.d.ts declares runPmCli and _testOnly, an object of 86 internal helpers; a bun install of the published 2026.8.16 artifact and an import of @unbrained/pm-cli/cli returns both at runtime, so the leak is in the shipped package and not only in the working tree.\n\nNegative control before: adding a new ./negative-control export to package.json left sdk-surface-snapshot --check, audit-package-boundary and package-sdk-contract-parity all passing, with the snapshot reporting '0 classified changes'.\n\nFix: listPublishedCodeExports derives the denominator from package.json exports and findUnclassifiedPackageCodeExports reports any that carry no classification; buildSdkSurfaceSnapshot refuses while the list is non-empty. '.' is classified aggregate_alias with ENTRYPOINT_ALIASES asserting its types path still equals ./sdk's, and its symbols are not duplicated (snapshot grew 6.7 KB, not 600 KB). './cli' is classified executable_entry and its two symbols are recorded, so the 86-helper signature is now signed contract data and any change to it is a classified surface change.\n\nNegative control after: the same injected export fails with 'Package export map publishes unclassified code entrypoints: ./negative-control', exit 1. Removing it restores the pass.\n\nVerification: tests/unit/scripts/sdk-surface-snapshot.spec.ts 17/17 pass, including a test that asserts the real repository export map is fully classified and that the snapshot's entrypoint set equals listPublishedCodeExports(package.json). Full suite passed. pnpm quality:static passed.\n\nThe separate question of whether ./cli should publish _testOnly at all is deliberately not answered here; pm-rf120g owns it."
files[3]{path,scope,note}:
  scripts/sdk-surface-snapshot.mjs,project,Derives the surface denominator from package.json exports and fails closed on unclassified code exports
  sdk/public-surface.json,project,Now records the root alias and the ./cli executable entry
  tests/unit/scripts/sdk-surface-snapshot.spec.ts,project,"Coverage for the export-map denominator,alias drift refusal,and the real repository export map"
